## 2. Migrating And Improving Creation Environment (Build Mode)

### Milestone 2.1 — Migrating to Godot
- [x] Get current unity builder verision into godot and fit the pieces (make it compatable with curent systems)


### Milestone 2.2 — Core build tools
- [x] Gizmos (move/rotate/scale/select) — use ImGuizmo or a close port rather than reinventing gizmo math
- [X] Object selection/sorting UI
- [x] GUI Gizmos/tools
- [ ] Gizmo snapping: toggleable increment snap for move (grid), rotate (angle) and scale, with configurable increments and a modifier-key override; the snap config lives in the toolbox (`GizmoMath.Snap` already exists — this is wiring + config UI, not new math)
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can enter build mode, fly around with freecam, select an object, and move/rotate/scale it with visible gizmo handles.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 moving · 🔴 smooth gizmos · 🟡 GUI creation tools · 🟡 increment snapping

### Milestone 2.3 — Inspector property system
- [ ] Scrollable Inspector section so long property lists stay usable
- [ ] Typed property widgets: checkbox (bool), dropdown (enum/choice), plus the existing numeric/text fields
- [ ] Per-object property set, starting with: Anchored, CanCollide, Texture
- [ ] Background picture property: apply an image as the lot background instead of the procedural sky. A file browser pops up and the user browses to the image; a clear action returns to the default sky
- [ ] Semantics for the two new part properties settled in code comments before the widgets land — what `CanCollide = false` does to the body (`CollisionShape3D.Disabled` vs. removing the shape), and what "Anchored" actually blocks (editor drag only, or every position write including Lua `SetPosition`)
- [ ] Properties are exposed through the bound Lua API, so scripts can read and set them (respecting the §1.1 boundary: no direct Godot access)
- [ ] Property widgets are data-driven (a property declares its type and options), so adding a new property doesn't require new Inspector UI code
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can select an object, scroll the Inspector, toggle Anchored/CanCollide with checkboxes, pick a Texture from a dropdown, and see the change take effect in the scene and in Lua.
**Difficulty:** 🟡 scrollable Inspector · 🟡 typed widgets · 🟠 data-driven property declaration · 🟠 Anchored/CanCollide semantics · 🔴 Texture + background picture (shared image-loading path, seeds §5.2)

### Milestone 2.4 — Editor workflow
- [ ] Undo/redo across gizmo drags, Inspector edits and hierarchy operations (command stack; `MarkDirty` is the only history today)
- [ ] Drag objects in the hierarchy panel to reorder, and drag one object into another to reparent (`Reparent` exists; the panel has clicks + marquee only)
- [ ] Autosave and crash recovery — **depends on §8.1's `.lot` format**; nothing exists to serialize yet
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can undo and redo any edit, reorder and reparent by dragging in the hierarchy, and recover their lot after a crash or restart without losing work.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 undo/redo · 🟠 hierarchy drag/reparent · 🔴 autosave/crash recovery (blocked on §8.1)

### Milestone 2.5 — Lighting and environment settings
- [ ] Time of day (sun angle + colour), fog, and sky presets in the creation environment, replacing the fixed procedural sky (`BuilderScene.BuildViewport`)
- [ ] Environment settings persisted as lot metadata — **depends on §8.1**
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator sets time of day, fog and a sky preset in build mode and sees the same lighting when the lot is loaded and played.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 environment controls · 🟠 persistence (blocked on §8.1)

