## 5. Characters, 3D meshes

*Capsule prototyping moved to §3.4 — it is a runtime concern (Test mode needs a controllable character to be meaningful), not an art/asset one.*

### Milestone 5.1 — Rigged characters
- [ ] R6-style rig support
- [ ] Body part tagging
- [ ] .avlot format: accessories/3D mesh attachment
- [ ] .avlot format: animation tagging (walking/jumping/etc. — untagged animations won't function properly)
**Acceptance criteria:** A rigged character loads with attached accessories and plays a tagged walk/jump animation correctly triggered by movement state.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 R6 rig · 🟠 accessories/animation tagging

### Milestone 5.2 — Runtime GLTF/rigged mesh loading/ Accessory application
- [ ] Runtime loading of rigged 3D meshes (GLTF) with custom textures for characters/accessories
- [ ] Confirm GLTFDocument/GLTFState API + Load() pattern works end-to-end for OpenLot's asset pipeline
- [ ] Character Edit UI (Inside game creation Environment) Accessory placement, 2d clothing.
**Acceptance criteria:** A character rig with a custom texture loads at runtime from a GLTF file with no editor pre-import step.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 

