## 6. Animation System & Audio

*Custom systems, not Godot's built-in animation tooling.*

### Milestone 6.1 — .lanim format + tooling
- [ ] Animator UI (Roblox Animator-style)
- [ ] Real-time animation-to-code conversion
- [ ] Animation smoother, toggleable for a retro/choppy look option
- [ ] Apply this animation system to non-character objects too
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can key a simple animation in the Animator UI, export it as .lanim, and see it play correctly on a rigged character in-lot, with the smoother togglable.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 Animator UI · 🟠 real-time conversion · 🟡 smoother

### Milestone 6.2 — Audio system
- [ ] Sound playback/mixing, 3D positional audio, and an audio pool (no audio exists in the project today)
- [ ] Audio bound into the Lua API so scripts can play cues (verb-first methods per §2.2)
**Acceptance criteria:** A script can play a sound on an object and a player hears it positioned at that object in the lot.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 (nothing exists yet) · 🟠 Lua binding

