## 7. Networking

### Milestone 7.1 — Session model
- [ ] Host/join/list session model
- [ ] State sync across clients
**Acceptance criteria:** Two clients can join the same hosted lot and see each other's characters move in real time with acceptable sync.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 🔴 — highest-research items on the whole roadmap; budget real standalone research time here

### Milestone 7.2 — Decentralized/self-hosting model
- [ ] Peer-to-peer hosting path (free/default option, alongside Providers — see §11)
**Acceptance criteria:** A user can host a lot from their own machine and have it be joinable/discoverable without a Provider in the loop.
**Difficulty:** 🔴

### Milestone 7.3 — Chatting system
*(moved from §12 — chat is part of the playable core, not a post-MLP extra)*
- [ ] Chat Bubble support
- [ ] Chatting UI
- [ ] Private chat (P2P without messages hitting the server they are in) — depends on 7.1's transport; the two items above can land on the existing `LoopbackTransport` path first
**Acceptance criteria:** A player can send chat that others in the lot see as a bubble and in the chat UI, with private chat routed peer-to-peer.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 (bubbles/UI) · 🔴 (private P2P chat, until 7.1 exists)

---

## 8. Save/load & lot persistence

### Milestone 8.1 — .lot format & versioning
- [ ] Define the `.lot` schema and a format version field, plus the migration path for older files
- [ ] Define the serialized payload: 3D objects, lot UI elements (`LotUIRoot`), script references, and lot metadata (name, environment settings)
**Acceptance criteria:** The `.lot` format is documented and versioned, and a file written by an older build is either migrated or rejected with a clear error rather than failing silently.
**Difficulty:** 🟠

### Milestone 8.2 — Save/load
- [ ] Save a creation as a `.lot` file
- [ ] Load a saved creation, same device
- [ ] Transfer and load a saved creation on a different device (may be held for later)
**Acceptance criteria:** A lot built on one machine can be saved, copied to a second machine, and loaded there with all objects, UI elements and scripts intact.
**Difficulty:** 🟠

---

## 9. Testing & QA/ simple servers

### Milestone 9.1 — Tester team process
- [ ] Recruit/organize a small tester team
**Acceptance criteria:** A tester can report an issue through a defined channel and it's triaged before the next build.
**Difficulty:** 🟩 (Rolkka-owned directly)

### Milestone 9.2 — Networking bug reports into tester networking
- [ ] Define a lightweight bug-report/feedback loop through a channel the tester team owns
- [ ] Route it through an API so the team can triage incoming reports
**Difficulty:** 🟠

### Milestone 9.3 — In-client reporting
- [ ] Report a lot/player from in-client, routed into the §9.2 feedback channel with lot + client context attached
- [ ] Moderation policy and enforcement stay in Tier 1/2 plugins (§1.3) — the core exposes only the narrow enforcement primitives, never policy
**Acceptance criteria:** A player can report a lot from inside it and the report reaches the triage channel with enough context to act on.
**Difficulty:** 🟠

