# POST MLP

## 10. Modding / Plugin System

### Milestone 10.1 — Tier 1: Terminal apps
- [ ] Package-manager-style install command (apt-like)
- [ ] Sandboxed execution inside the terminal via its own API only
**Acceptance criteria:** A third-party terminal app installs via the package manager and runs correctly without touching anything outside the terminal API surface.
**Difficulty:** 🟠

### Milestone 10.2 — Tier 2: Creation-environment plugins
- [ ] Package-manager install path shared with Tier 1
- [ ] Defined plugin API extending build-mode (tools/panels/importers)
**Acceptance criteria:** A sample plugin adds a new tool/panel to build mode using only the published plugin API.
**Difficulty:** 🟠

### Milestone 10.3 — Tier 3: Deep/engine-level plugins
- [ ] Document the boundary where Tier 3 plugins reach past OpenLot's API into Godot itself
- [ ] Custom optimization/shader plugin support
**Acceptance criteria:** A documented example shows a Tier 3 plugin modifying rendering behavior directly, with clear docs on what's supported vs. unsupported.
**Difficulty:** 🔴

---

## 11. Providers & Platform Economy

*Separate from free peer-to-peer hosting (§7.2), which remains available.*

### Milestone 11.1 — Provider system core
- [ ] Provider listing/discovery mechanism (third parties list games on their own discoverable list)
- [ ] Provider-managed hosting path as an alternative to self-hosting
- [ ] Per-provider configurable ToS, pricing, rules, moderation policy, age-safety tier
- [ ] Liability model: explicitly provider-owned, not OpenLot-owned, reflected in docs/ToS templates
**Acceptance criteria:** A third-party provider can register, set their own rules/pricing/age-tier, and list/host a game, with OpenLot's own docs clearly scoping liability to the provider.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 (new, largely undesigned below the concept level)

### Milestone 11.2 — Official OpenLot provider
- [ ] Stand up Rolkka's own instance as the official provider
- [ ] Self-custody USDC flow for creator payouts (wallet-to-wallet, no provider custody)
- [ ] No minor monetization at launch — minors earn/buy only through a parent-held wallet
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator on the official provider can receive a USDC payment directly to their own wallet with the provider never holding funds in the loop.
**Difficulty:** 🔴 (custody-avoidant design already settled; implementation still open)

### Milestone 11.3 — Monetization features (official provider)
- [ ] Managed hosting tiers (bandwidth/storage tiers, priority slots)
- [ ] Discovery/promoted placement in game listings
- [ ] Creator "Pro" subscription tier (extra plugin slots, higher limits, analytics)
- [ ] Player "Plus" subscription tier (cosmetic perks, exclusive access)
- [ ] (Later stage) B2B "OpenLot Cloud" hosted backend infra + consulting for third-party providers
**Acceptance criteria:** A creator can subscribe to Pro and immediately see raised limits/analytics access; a player can subscribe to Plus and receive a cosmetic perk.
**Difficulty:** 🟠 hosting tiers/subscriptions · 🔴 B2B infra (post-MLP, needs an actual provider ecosystem first)

### Milestone 11.4 — Official plugins (post-MLP stage)
- [ ] Ko-fi / Patreon API integration plugin for gamepasses/paid games
- [ ] Roblox compatibility tools, staged least-to-most advanced (Lua API shim scoping, R6/R15 rig mapping research, asset importer)
- [ ] "Bender" — precise object-bending creation tool
- [ ] (More TBD as MLP usage reveals gaps)
**Acceptance criteria:** Ko-fi/Patreon plugin lets a creator gate a paid game/gamepass without OpenLot ever touching payment custody; Roblox compat tier list published even if only partial shimming is implemented.
**Difficulty:** 🟡 Ko-fi/Patreon · 🔴 Roblox compat (start scoping/research early, don't wait for "last stage" to begin) · 🟠 Bender

